    source:{ name:"Illinois Department of Financial and Professional Regulation", handle:"IL DFPR", platform:"web", kind:"gov" },
    text:"Illinois became the first U.S. state to mandate independent third-party safety audits of frontier AI models, requiring model developers to submit to annual audits by accredited third parties before deployment of systems above a specified capability threshold. The requirement takes effect January 1, 2027 and applies to models trained on more than 1e26 floating-point operations.",
